            <ArticleTitle>Sacral Tarlov cyst: surgical treatment by clipping.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>381-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.wneu.2012.06.015</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1878-8750(12)00635-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">This study reports the anatomopathological classification of Tarlov cysts and the various treatment techniques described in the literature.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The authors present their patient series (19 cases) with a long follow-up (range 9 months to 25 years) treated by cyst remodeling around the root using titanium clips.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The technique is effective in both avoiding cerebrospinal fluid leakage and resolving bladder dysfunction when urinary symptoms are incomplete and discontinuous.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The clipping technique for Tarlov cysts is easy, valid, safe, rapid, and effective.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2013 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
